SUMMARY:The Neon Room at Helium: Hunter Donaldson & Jake Silberman Show
LOCATION:Portland
DESCRIPTION:Join former Portland favorites Jake Silberman and Hunter Donald
 son as they return from New York for one night only!\n\nHunter Donaldson is
  a comedian\, podcast host\, streamer and writer living in New York. His lo
 ve of strategy board games is covered extensively on his podcast "Space Cat
 s Peace Turtles\," which is supported by over 1500 patrons on Patreon and h
 as been featured in Polygon\, Geek and Sundry\, and The Dice Tower. As a co
 median\, Hunter has performed across the country and has brought his podcas
 t to headline comedy clubs in Indianapolis\, Portland\, and soon many more.
  As a streamer and video producer\, Hunter has built a considerable audienc
 e as a Twitch and Youtube partner with lifetime viewership well over one mi
 llion.\n\nCalled a “true comedian” by legend Katt Williams and “incre
 dibly talented” by Nick Mullen\, Jake Silberman is a New York City comedi
 an who has been relentlessly touring the country over the last four years. 
 He’s headlined numerous clubs including Helium\, House of Comedy and the 
 Comedy Club of Kansas\, while also opening for some of the biggest names in
  stand up including Mark Normand\, Jordan Jensen and regularly opening for 
 Kyle Kinane. Jake’s latest special “Live from Portland” showcases his
  sharp and biting material as well as his ability to mix in improvisational
  moments. Jake’s work has been featured on Amazon Prime\, Tom Segura and 
 Christina P’s popular “Your Mom’s House” podcast as well as “Now 
 This News.'' He was voted “Funniest Person in Portland'' while living the
 re\, and has performed on numerous festivals around the country\, including
  the 10\,000 Laughs and Red Clay comedy festivals. When in New York\, Jake 
 can be found performing in numerous clubs across the city.\n\nManagement re
 serves the right to prevent customers from entering the facility who they d
